670 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (Make a schedule!!! Be super extra and set out how many questions you're going to do each day, set out how many anki cards for you to review, how many Kaplan chapters to read etc etc. like be so specific because then when you finish that you stop. If you have no direction for your day you won't balance breaks and studying. Its so helpful to know what you're going to do every day and do only that then have fun after.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
671 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (I cannot emphasize this enough: do as many practice questions as possible. Prioritize questions because then you will be exposed to all the content and how it will be tested which is way more helpful than content review. Also trust what you know and what you have learned in your classes even if its not directly what is taught in the MCAT textbooks.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
672 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (MCAT is not just mentally tasking but physically, so prioritize having a rest day. Even if you are behind! It is a marathon, not a race, so taking care of your well-being is super important. Take care of yourself, take breaks, and be kind to yourself. You are doing a really hard thing and likely have a whole school year ahead of you, so do not burn out too quick!)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
673 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 281 0 R
/E (No matter what happens on test day, be SOOOO proud of yourself! The grind is going to be taxing and discouraging, but this is one step closer to your dream. So have faith in yourself, and be so so proud of what you have accomplished!)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
